[2026-10-10T10:55:08] CHAT
Q: What is adaptive concretization?
A: Adaptive concretization is a program synthesis technique that enables efficient parallelization of challenging synthesis problems. It involves dynamically identifying which unknowns in a synthesis problem are best suited for explicit search versus symbolic search through constraint solving. The main idea is to partially concretize a randomly chosen, but likely influential, subset of the unknowns to be synthesized. This technique combines the strengths of both symbolic and explicit search strategies, allowing for a more effective search process. It has been shown to outperform traditional synthesis methods in many cases and supports good parallel scalability.
Sources: DBLP conf cav JeonQSF15 (2015); DBLP journals fmsd JeonQSF17 (2017)
